1.22.1: the D610's image area, which declares no crop

1.22.0 cut raw files to the image area the file declares, and the
D610 declares none: its CropHiSpeed tag reads "6080x4028 cropped to
6080x4028 at 0,0", so the masked border stayed. Bodies that declare
nothing now get their image area from a small table keyed by model
and raw size (D600/D610 6016x4016 from 6080x4028; D3200/D3300, D7000,
D800, D90 and D750 from memory, each guarded by an exact raw-size
match so a mismatch means no crop, never a wrong one), and only the
side of the masked band is read from the samples: of the two
candidate bands, the one at the black level is the mask. A generic
"find the black border" detector was tried and dropped - it cropped
a legitimately black edge column in the test scene, which a real
photo can have too.

The table lookup and the side choice are unit-tested on a 40x30
readout masked on either side; the bordered synthetic raws of 1.22.0
still decode to the bit as the plain files.

